BSP-Yocto-IndComms-IBV-AM64x-v0.1                    2026-01-05
==================================================================

- Based on BSP-Yocto-Ampliphy-AM64x-PD25.2.0 and IBV IndComms SDK v1.2 (based on
  TI INDUSTRIAL-COMMUNICATIONS-SDK-AM64X 11.00.00.13)
- Linux kernel v6.12.8-phy7
- U-Boot v2025.07-phy5
- Yocto 5.0.15 (Scarthgap)
- meta-indcomms-ibv (tag v1.2-phy1)


Tested Yocto images:
--------------------

- ampliphy/phytec-indcomms-image
  * phyboard-electra-am64xx-2


Build environment:
------------------

- Ubuntu 24.04 64-bit


Features:
---------

- support of phyCORE-AM64x Industrial Communication Kit
- demo firmware for EtherCAT, PROFINET und EtherNet/IP (running on R5F/PRU)
- using either carrier board PHY or extension board PHY
- ADC input to/LED output from R5F
- sharing information from/to Linux using a helper software


Known Issues
------------

- adding/enabling DT overlays via '/boot/overlays.txt' does work in principle,
  yet the Yocto build step for this is broken. One needs to create the file manually.
- OE welcome message only lists 'phytec-headless-image' as tested build target;
  message generally broken in scarthgap
